cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software or the Fisher-MoE method, please cite the
  EMNLP 2026 paper below.
title: >-
  Less is MoE: Trimming Experts in Domain-Specialist Language Models
abstract: >-
  Official implementation of Fisher-MoE: intra-expert structured pruning and
  compression for Mixture-of-Experts (MoE) large language models. Prunes FFN
  intermediate dimensions ranked by Fisher importance instead of dropping or
  merging whole experts, preserving general-purpose capability at a 50%
  compression ratio while reducing weight memory by ~45% and improving
  inference throughput by 21%.
type: software
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: https://github.com/HectorHHZ/Less-is-MoE
url: https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.05538
keywords:
  - mixture-of-experts
  - moe
  - expert-pruning
  - model-compression
  - structured-pruning
  - large-language-models
  - efficient-inference
  - fisher-information
